// dolibarr_main_dolcrypt_key
// ==========================
// An secret key to encrypt/decrypt data with the dolcrypt() method, for reversible encryption.
// This value is also never visible and never propagated outside of Dolibarr, it is used as key for the dolcrypt encryption.
// If you restore a complete system backup (from a SQL dump), you must also restore this value because some data are encrypted into database by using this key.
// WARNING: Changing this value will make some sensitive encrypted values in database wrong (no way to read it without the correct key, so you
// must also save this key when you make a database backup).
// Default value: ''. When not defined, the $dolibarr_main_instance_unique_id will be used instead.
// Examples:
// $dolibarr_main_dolcrypt_key='';
//
$dolibarr_main_dolcrypt_key='';


// dolibarr_main_instance_unique_id
// ================================
// An ID that is unique for each installation.
// This value is also never visible and never propagated outside of Dolibarr. It can be used as a salt/key for some encryption (For example to get
// a unique hashed key for URLs, application will hash the value to hash concatenated with this string. Example: sha256('dolibarr'+dolibarr_main_instance_unique_id)
// Default value: randomly defined during installation
// Examples:
// $dolibarr_main_instance_unique_id='84b5bc91f83b56e458db71e0adac2b62';
//
$dolibarr_main_instance_unique_id='84b5bc91f83b56e458db71e0adac2b62';


